Hi, Coverity turned up the following:

```
*** CID 1517823:  Integer handling issues  (OVERFLOW_BEFORE_WIDEN)
/builds/wireshark/wireshark/epan/dissectors/packet-dect-nwk.c: 2781 in fmt_dect_nwk_ipei()
2775     	guint64 digit_divisor, ipei_digits;
2776     
2777     	emc = ( ( ipei & 0xFFFF00000 ) >> 20 ) & 0xFFFF;
2778     	psn = ipei & 0xFFFFF;
2779     
2780     	digit_divisor = 100000000000;
>>>     CID 1517823:  Integer handling issues  (OVERFLOW_BEFORE_WIDEN)
>>>     Potentially overflowing expression "emc * 10000000" with type "int" (32 bits, signed) is evaluated using 32-bit arithmetic, and then used in a context that expects an expression of type "guint64" (64 bits, unsigned).
2781     	ipei_digits = emc * 10000000 + psn;
2782     	check_digit = 0;
2783     	for(guint8 i = 1; i <= 12; i++) {
2784     		check_digit += (guint16)( ( ipei_digits / digit_divisor ) * i );
2785     		ipei_digits = ipei_digits % digit_divisor;
2786     		digit_divisor /= 10;
```

